&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field, with at least two years of relevant experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in IFRS (International Financial Reporting Standards) and general accounting principles; skilled in Microsoft Office applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented with a proactive work attitude; intermediate to advanced English proficiency and willingness to work with English materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love It&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance review (2 times a year)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private medical insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual leaves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sick, compassionate and special leaves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All-hands meeting at overseas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TGIF, monthly birthday and other fun events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

